    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DjHKVMQmvVnXWZYx2E2crb)_\n\n**Before:** `org-ql` was installed in `sp-org-base`, and `org-super-agenda`, which `org-ql` requires, a few modules later in `sp-org-agenda`. Elpaca queued it as a dependency first and warned `org-super-agenda previously queued as dependency of: (org-ql)`. `emr` (in `sp-prog-misc`) had the same problem with `paredit`, installed by `sp-lisp` further down the list. Every module loaded during startup.\n\n**After:**\n- `org-ql` moves to `sp-org-agenda`, right after `org-super-agenda` (`.el` and the literate doc).\n- `sp-lisp` loads before `sp-prog-misc`.\n- Twelve leaf modules (`sp-academic`, `sp-dgraphs`, `sp-relationship-annotator`, `sp-notes`, `sp-semantic`, `sp-dyn-graph`, `sp-sandbox`, `sp-vcontrol`, `sp-magit-style`, `sp-terminal`, `sp-eshell`, `sp-ai`) are in `lem--late-modules` and load 0.5 s after Emacs first goes idle once Elpaca has finished its queues. `sp-defer-late-modules` = `nil` loads them with the rest. No other module requires them.\n- `docs/load-order.org` (linked from `docs/main.org`) has two Graphviz graphs (rendered SVGs beside it), the table of requirements behind each arrow, and a checklist for placing a new module. CHANGELOG entry added under a \"Startup and module load order\" set.\n\n**Checked:** Emacs 29.3 reads `init.el` and the changed modules; the module list is the same set as before; the late-module functions ran against stubs (twelve modules required in order, queues processed). The requirements come from the `Package-Requires` headers of `org-ql`, `org-super-agenda`, `emr`, `org-ref`, `org-gtd`, `org-node`, `code-review`, `vulpea-ui`, `treemacs`, `claude-code`, `gptel-agent` and others, read from GitHub.\n\n**Not checked:** a real startup. Elpaca cannot reach MELPA from the container, so I have not seen the warning disappear, nor that the late modules install and configure their packages after init (I read `elpaca.el`, which suggests they do once `elpaca-process-queues` is called). Keys defined only in late modules (for example `C-M-g` for magit) work from about a second after startup. Duplicate explicit declarations (`hl-todo`, `org-autolist`, `elisp-demos`, `company`) are left alone.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_015tcMWj1Z6j2uCgMRYPBfDN)_",
